export anchor ThermostatDialStyle:
    number: 375
    screen: SmartHome
    name: Thermostat dial
    idea: One big round thermostat dial for the living room leads the screen, the other rooms sit around it as small ring gauges, and even the day's energy is drawn as a 24 hour clock face.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #141416, page ground
        body: #1c1c20, room cards, cards and the dial rim
        well: #232328, stat rows, scene discs and fields
        line: #34343b, card borders and dial edge
        ink: #f3f1ee, text and the dial reading
        mute: #aeaab2, labels, meta and dial numerals
        heat: #ff9a5c, lit dial ticks, warm rings, the active scene and primary button
        onHeat: #2b1306, text and icons on heat
        cool: #7cc4ff, cool rings, low hour sectors and focus
        ok: #8fe0a8, locked ring and battery
        warn: #ffc65c, motion ring and the garage alert
    type:
        A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
        then system-ui. Base 15px at 1.5. The dial reading is 88px at 300
        with a 32px raised degree sign, stat figures 22px at 700, room names
        16px at 700, meta 14px muted and chips 12px at 700.
    layout:
        A header row holds a small knob mark with Brightwork Home, the day
        and time, and on the right a pill shaped alert outlined in yellow
        with Garage door open for 2 hours and an orange pill Close now. The
        stage below is a three column grid with a 440px round thermostat
        dial in the centre for the living room. The dial has 81 ticks over a
        270 degree sweep from 10 to 30 degrees, lit orange up to 21.5 with
        an orange marker dot, numerals every 5, and a dark inner face
        showing Living room, 21.5 and lines for 3 lights on at 40 percent
        and TV off. Two room cards sit left and two right, each a pill ended
        card with a 76px ring gauge, blue for kitchen at 20.0, orange for
        bedroom at 19.0 with a heating chip, and green lock and yellow
        walker rings for the front door and the garden. Below, a wide Energy
        today card pairs a 24 hour clock face chart, one radial sector per
        hour with midnight at the top, orange for hours of 0.7 kWh or more
        and blue below, beside three stat rows for used, solar and a battery
        bar. A Scenes card holds four 72px round discs with Movie filled
        orange and marked On now. Below 1080px the dial goes on top with
        rooms two by two, and at phone width everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between the dial, the rooms and the cards, 20 to 24px card padding.
    density: Low. One reading dominates and four rooms orbit it.
    corners:
        Everything round. 28px cards, full pills for chips, buttons and
        fields, circles for gauges, discs and swatches.
    borders: 1px #34343b on cards, 1.5px currentColor on chips and the alert.
    shadows: None, except a 6px soft orange ring around the active scene disc.
    icons:
        Round line icons at 2px stroke, 18 to 26px. States pair a word with
        a clock, check, walking figure or dash circle.
    focus: A 3px cool blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Warm and short, such as On now, Energy today and Close now.
